<title>INDIA: Delhi shares surge 2.8 pct at settlement start.</title>
<headline>Delhi shares surge 2.8 pct at settlement start.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Strong buying by foreign financial institutions and domestic mutual funds at the start of a new settlement period pushed Delhi share prices to a sharply higher close on Monday, brokers said.</p>
<p>The Delhi Stock Exchange's benchmark index closed 25.15 points, or 2.8 percent, higher at 937.13 points.</p>
</text>
